Interesting: the base64 parser broke because splitting the cookie on `.` is unsafe when the cookie value is quoted/escaped or gets truncated by `=` handling. I'll modify the probe to print the raw cookie and parse more robustly. The observed lengths 60 and 66 also show the flag length can be inferred from `len(username) + 9 + len(flag)`, suggesting the flag is around 51 bytes if username 0 gives 60 total.
